# Shot list for KD-001, in the form the generator consumes.
#
# One shot per line:  <positive prompt> TAB <colours to suppress>
#
# The style and environment blocks in shared/tools/wan-still.py are prepended
# to every line, so they are not repeated here - that is what keeps the shots
# looking like one object in one room.
#
# REWRITTEN after rendering the first version. Five of eight shots were
# usable; the three failures all broke the same rule, so the rule is now
# followed here rather than restated:
#
#   ONE character doing ONE thing. The old shot 7 put two characters, four
#   objects and a described action in one frame and the model abandoned the
#   vinyl-toy style entirely for a flat sticker on a seascape - the same
#   collapse that generating at 640 produced. It is now Noor's paw entering
#   the frame and resting on Samsam's head: one subject, one gesture, and
#   better blocking besides, since the script's own line is that the camera
#   stays on the face that knows the answer.
#
#   NO ABSTRACT OBJECTS. "Four ceramic pieces" meant nothing to the model, so
#   it gave them eyes and made them creatures. The pieces are now described as
#   what they were - halves of a broken blue cup, with the handle still on one
#   of them - which the model has seen.
#
#   NO SUBJECT THE SHOT DOES NOT NEED. The old shot 4 asked for an empty table
#   edge AND the kitten, and got the kitten standing on the table like a
#   figurine. The shot is about absence, so the kitten is gone from it and the
#   cup's absence carries it.
#
# The negative column is per shot and not optional. Measured: a plain "red
# scarf" generated yellow twice, so the kitten's shots push yellow out. The
# two shots that also carry Noor's yellow CANNOT, because yellow is her own
# signature - there the red has to win on repetition alone.
#
# "sharp shards, broken glass" on shots 7 and 8 is a children's-content
# compliance constraint, not a style choice: the pieces are ceramic with
# rounded edges and a paw touches one of them.

extreme close up of two small white rabbit paws hugging a blue ceramic cup with rounded edges against the chest, a white rabbit in a bright yellow raincoat, warm window light	orange, sharp shards, broken glass
close up of a blue ceramic cup with rounded edges standing alone at the very edge of a light wooden table, soft shadow beside it	orange, sharp shards, broken glass, hands, paws
extreme close up of the face of a small round grey kitten wearing a small narrow crimson red scarf tied neatly around its neck, scarlet red, big dark glossy eyes open wide, one grey paw reaching slowly forward	yellow, yellow scarf, orange scarf, pink scarf
close up of the empty edge of a light wooden table, nothing on it, a faint clean ring where a cup stood, soft daylight	pink, purple, yellow, cat, kitten, rabbit, cup
extreme close up of the face of a small round grey kitten wearing a small narrow crimson red scarf, scarlet red, big dark glossy eyes lowered, quiet guilty expression, soft warm light	yellow, yellow scarf, orange scarf, pink scarf
close up of a small round grey kitten wearing a small narrow crimson red scarf, scarlet red, lifting its head to face the camera, big dark glossy eyes, calm hopeful expression	yellow, yellow scarf, orange scarf, pink scarf
close up of a small round grey kitten wearing a small narrow crimson red scarf, scarlet red, with one white rabbit paw in a bright yellow sleeve resting gently on top of its head, warm light	orange, sharp shards, broken glass, pink background
close up from above of two large curved halves of a broken blue ceramic cup lying on a light wooden floor, the cup handle still attached to one half, smooth rounded edges, one small grey kitten paw touching one half	orange, sharp shards, broken glass, yellow, eyes, face, creature
